WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.540 --> 00:00:05.500
One of them won «Melodi Grand Prix» and the other won «Melodifestivalen».

00:00:05.720 --> 00:00:10.640
Please welcome Alexander Rybak and Benjamin Ingrosso!

00:00:30.980 --> 00:00:32.980
Benjamin, do you remember ...

00:00:33.140 --> 00:00:38.000
... where you were when he won the international final last time?

00:00:38.100 --> 00:00:39.460
Yeah, I actually do!

00:00:39.460 --> 00:00:40.840
Don't say that you weren't born!

00:00:41.020 --> 00:00:41.820
No!

00:00:45.260 --> 00:00:46.380
How old were you?

00:00:47.300 --> 00:00:49.060
I had just learnt to speak.

00:00:49.060 --> 00:00:49.980
No, I'm joking.

00:00:50.120 --> 00:00:53.700
Let's see. It was around ten years ago, right?

00:00:53.700 --> 00:00:54.620
Nine.

00:00:54.740 --> 00:00:56.480
I was 11. 10-11 years old.

00:00:56.840 --> 00:01:01.680
I was actually at Carola's house, watching Eurovision Song Contest.

00:01:01.840 --> 00:01:03.160
Because ...

00:01:07.840 --> 00:01:09.280
So we have ...

00:01:09.280 --> 00:01:14.840
... Pernilla Wahlgrens son is sitting at Carola's house, watching the Eurovision Song Contest?

00:01:14.840 --> 00:01:17.420
It doesn't become more Eurovision than that?

00:01:17.420 --> 00:01:24.360
No! But I'm an old friend of her son's. So we had been watching a movie about Jesus the entire evening, actually.

00:01:24.460 --> 00:01:27.500
And eaten macaroni with sausage and ketchup.

00:01:27.500 --> 00:01:30.860
Which I as an Italian am a little skeptical about, pasta and ketchup, you know ...

00:01:31.140 --> 00:01:33.780
And I remember that I was like ...

00:01:34.060 --> 00:01:35.900
«Wow, that's really good!»

00:01:35.900 --> 00:01:39.720
And I ran out in their garden and pretended to be Alexander after that.

00:01:40.980 --> 00:01:43.220
«I'm in love with a fairytale ...»

00:01:43.220 --> 00:01:45.140
I thought it was a great song!

00:01:45.240 --> 00:01:45.960
Thank you!

00:01:47.980 --> 00:01:51.900
Alexander, how would you say that that success changed you?

00:01:52.600 --> 00:01:54.280
... and your personality?

00:01:56.260 --> 00:01:58.020
Me or my personality?

00:01:58.020 --> 00:01:59.400
Your personality!

00:01:59.700 --> 00:02:04.120
It's really easy to lose yourself in the middle of all this.

00:02:05.120 --> 00:02:06.660
How did it happen?

00:02:06.920 --> 00:02:08.260
Well, it ...

00:02:09.060 --> 00:02:10.500
For instance ...

00:02:10.500 --> 00:02:14.700
For instance, a friend of mine asked if we should do a football evening.

00:02:14.900 --> 00:02:20.420
And I replied: «Football evening?! Did you not see what happened in Eurovision?!»

00:02:20.420 --> 00:02:21.520
«I don't have time for ...»

00:02:21.520 --> 00:02:22.960
So, you say stupid things.

00:02:24.160 --> 00:02:26.280
So I think you are ...

00:02:26.320 --> 00:02:29.020
... more prepared, actually. You're 20?

00:02:29.020 --> 00:02:29.720
20, yes.

00:02:29.720 --> 00:02:34.000
You seem professional, and you have both your head and your heart in the right place.

00:02:34.000 --> 00:02:38.460
There's something about ... You have this in common, the two of you ... That you ...

00:02:38.560 --> 00:02:42.140
You've been somewhat wonder children.

00:02:42.160 --> 00:02:44.860
And stars since you were quite young.

00:02:46.680 --> 00:02:50.540
And you did musicals and were doing stuff at a very young age.

00:02:50.540 --> 00:02:51.320
Yes, exactly.

00:02:51.320 --> 00:02:52.700
Who were you in school?

00:02:52.920 --> 00:02:56.660
In school? Wow. I was quite different in school.

00:02:57.300 --> 00:03:00.180
I wasn't the smartest in class, and ...

00:03:00.640 --> 00:03:03.860
I loved everything that didn't have anything to do with school.

00:03:03.920 --> 00:03:08.240
I had different periods of being different roles when I was a kid.

00:03:08.240 --> 00:03:11.400
I was never myself. I was «Vanheden» in «Jönssonligan» for half a year.

00:03:11.400 --> 00:03:12.540
Yes, I've also been him!

00:03:13.080 --> 00:03:15.000
Short trousers and loafers!

00:03:17.280 --> 00:03:18.880
That's «Olsenbanden»!

00:03:20.180 --> 00:03:21.300
What did you say?

00:03:21.300 --> 00:03:22.120
«Jönssonligan.»

00:03:22.120 --> 00:03:23.260
«Olsenbanden» in Norwegian.

00:03:25.700 --> 00:03:27.320
We're gonna talk about those later.

00:03:27.660 --> 00:03:30.480
Anyways, so then I dressed up as «Vanheden» with a hat.

00:03:30.480 --> 00:03:32.880
And I was him. I went into character.

00:03:32.880 --> 00:03:34.960
And I was James Bond for a while.

00:03:34.960 --> 00:03:40.100
And then I was John Travolta. I dyed my hair black and wrote in a black dot on my chin.

00:03:40.100 --> 00:03:41.940
So in all my class photos ...

00:03:41.980 --> 00:03:43.900
Were you very popular, or ..?

00:03:43.900 --> 00:03:45.680
No, no, no, I had no friends.

00:03:45.980 --> 00:03:51.420
And the problem was that the teachers weren't the nicest either, because they ...

00:03:51.780 --> 00:03:52.500
They ...

00:03:52.800 --> 00:03:57.520
Because I seldom understood when we had math and subjects like that ...

00:03:57.520 --> 00:04:04.300
... I would try to tell them that I didn't understand, but they always thought that I was playing dumb.

00:04:04.300 --> 00:04:06.980
So it ended up with me being that ...

00:04:07.040 --> 00:04:09.280
... strange kid who is just weird.

00:04:09.460 --> 00:04:15.300
But when you wanted to entertain and be funny, did no one want to be in the audience thern, or ..?

00:04:15.500 --> 00:04:22.360
So I went to a very fancy school in Östermalm in Stockholm, and ...

00:04:22.360 --> 00:04:26.180
... in that school, it's not cool with culture and stuff like that.

00:04:26.220 --> 00:04:28.540
I didn't fit in from the beginning.

00:04:28.580 --> 00:04:32.540
It was the same school as our princess Victoria went to.

00:04:32.540 --> 00:04:34.680
There's not a lot of «Vanheden» there.

00:04:34.680 --> 00:04:36.580
No, there were no «Vanheden»s there at all.

00:04:41.220 --> 00:04:46.220
How strict was it for you when it comes to discipline?

00:04:47.660 --> 00:04:52.900
I come from a country, Belarus, where there is a lot of discipline.

00:04:53.020 --> 00:04:58.180
In Belarus, you learn to write and read when you're three.

00:04:59.180 --> 00:05:04.620
But my parents mixed this discipline with a lot of cleverness and love.

00:05:04.920 --> 00:05:06.100
So they ...

00:05:06.780 --> 00:05:08.820
How did they get you to practice?

00:05:09.380 --> 00:05:14.260
They were quite smart. When I realised that the other children didn't ...

00:05:14.260 --> 00:05:16.980
... have to practice two hours very day after school ...

00:05:16.980 --> 00:05:21.880
They said: «But if continue, you'll get this big set of Legos» and  things like that.

00:05:21.880 --> 00:05:26.120
They were very smart, because I then felt like I had something ...

00:05:26.200 --> 00:05:28.200
... to reach for, always.

00:05:28.280 --> 00:05:30.040
And it was great.

00:05:30.280 --> 00:05:35.060
But I felt different. And I think that children in school will feel like that no matter what.

00:05:35.180 --> 00:05:39.460
But I remember coming home crying to my dad ...

00:05:39.460 --> 00:05:45.480
And I said: «Dad, I'm doing something completely different from everyone else, and they don't understand me.»

00:05:45.480 --> 00:05:46.640
And he said to me:

00:05:47.320 --> 00:05:53.460
«As people, we're just generally scared of everything that's different.»

00:05:53.580 --> 00:05:57.360
«We're scared of things that are different.»

00:05:57.360 --> 00:06:02.180
«And you have to believe in yourself, and believe in the things that are different about you. And if you believe in that ...»

00:06:02.180 --> 00:06:05.540
«The others will also believe that after a while.»

00:06:05.540 --> 00:06:08.500
And that was so important for me to hear, from my dad.

00:06:12.000 --> 00:06:14.680
Were you also different as a child?

00:06:14.680 --> 00:06:19.260
Yes. I was also «Vanheden», but I also changed between him and «Dynamit-Harry» quite a lot.

00:06:19.520 --> 00:06:21.380
And «Papphammar»!

00:06:21.380 --> 00:06:23.760
But I guess I was quite ...

00:06:24.400 --> 00:06:27.260
I also played a lot of roles. I was quite ...

00:06:27.620 --> 00:06:29.840
... overweight as a child.

00:06:29.940 --> 00:06:33.940
... and so my way of being included, was to be funny.

00:06:34.060 --> 00:06:35.500
... at my own expense.

00:06:35.500 --> 00:06:39.060
So, I would be funny about myself before anyone had the chance to tease me.

00:06:39.060 --> 00:06:40.860
I had to be funny first, simply.

00:06:40.860 --> 00:06:43.440
And that was a hard school to be a part of.

00:06:43.580 --> 00:06:45.580
Humour-wise.

00:06:45.580 --> 00:06:48.040
And then you have to recapture yourself, to sort of ...

00:06:48.040 --> 00:06:50.200
... feel like you're not selling yourself short. But it was ...

00:06:50.840 --> 00:06:52.440
... exactly the same ...

00:06:52.620 --> 00:06:56.980
«Vanheden» is grateful to work with.

00:06:57.280 --> 00:06:59.040
You were ...

00:06:59.240 --> 00:07:03.780
You mentioned your Russian background, and you're half Italian ...

00:07:03.780 --> 00:07:04.500
Ingrosso.

00:07:04.580 --> 00:07:05.080
Yes.

00:07:05.080 --> 00:07:06.440
You still live at home?

00:07:06.460 --> 00:07:07.740
Yes, I live at home.

00:07:07.920 --> 00:07:10.320
So you're living this teenage life?

00:07:10.760 --> 00:07:15.640
Yes, I am! But I cook the food at home, so I'm responsible for that.

00:07:16.240 --> 00:07:17.940
Thanks, thanks!

00:07:18.120 --> 00:07:21.340
Do you still have posters in your room?

00:07:21.880 --> 00:07:23.880
If I've had posters in my room?

00:07:23.880 --> 00:07:25.600
Yeah, do you still have your teenage posters there?

00:07:25.600 --> 00:07:26.280
Yes.

00:07:27.120 --> 00:07:32.880
My songwriting colleagues were at my place once, and we were going to eat dinner and ...

00:07:32.880 --> 00:07:37.740
They were completely shocked when they entered my room, because the hadn't thought about that I was ...

00:07:37.740 --> 00:07:38.860
19-20 years old.

00:07:38.860 --> 00:07:40.940
So when they came into my room, they were like ...

00:07:41.280 --> 00:07:43.420
«Eh. Benjamin, you're 12.»

00:07:43.820 --> 00:07:47.520
I still have my stuff from when I was younger.

00:07:47.600 --> 00:07:49.120
I have to have, like ...

00:07:49.500 --> 00:07:52.700
A Batman doll up on my shelf and things like that.

00:07:52.700 --> 00:07:54.480
And a «Jönssonligan» poster.

00:07:55.100 --> 00:07:57.800
But I like it. I think it's ...

00:07:57.820 --> 00:07:59.020
I think it's nice.

00:07:59.020 --> 00:08:00.820
Did you have any posters on the wall?

00:08:01.340 --> 00:08:04.660
I've still got my old bedroom back at my parent's house.

00:08:04.820 --> 00:08:08.080
And there I've got all the ... I had more ...

00:08:08.080 --> 00:08:10.680
... pictures of beautiful women, really.

00:08:11.140 --> 00:08:13.440
Jennifer Love Hewitt ...

00:08:14.340 --> 00:08:16.400
What's her name? Angelina Jolie.

00:08:16.500 --> 00:08:19.060
Pernilla Wahlgren, people like that.

00:08:21.340 --> 00:08:22.460
His mom!

00:08:26.900 --> 00:08:28.720
Who did you have?

00:08:28.740 --> 00:08:31.220
I'm thinking the same, who did I have?

00:08:31.340 --> 00:08:36.180
I was really bohemian. I had road signs that I had found and things like that.

00:08:36.320 --> 00:08:38.500
And tall hats and old ladders.

00:08:38.680 --> 00:08:41.160
And I think I had Michael Bolton!

00:08:42.720 --> 00:08:45.040
Exactly when he started to become bald up there.

00:08:46.620 --> 00:08:49.040
I also had Twisted Sisters.

00:08:49.120 --> 00:08:49.840
Wow. Good!

00:08:49.840 --> 00:08:54.160
You've got a good range with Twisted Sister and Michael Bolton, you're an open person?

00:08:54.160 --> 00:08:56.220
Yeah, just like that. I'm a mix of those two.

00:08:57.320 --> 00:09:03.460
You're on your way to Lisbon, you're going to compete against each other.

00:09:04.720 --> 00:09:06.760
And this is ...

00:09:06.760 --> 00:09:08.960
Is this the first time you're performing outside Sweden?

00:09:09.040 --> 00:09:10.280
Abroad?

00:09:10.960 --> 00:09:11.500
Yes.

00:09:11.580 --> 00:09:14.300
Yes. Professionally, yes. Absolutely.

00:09:14.300 --> 00:09:17.060
What do you mean? Have you performed privately?

00:09:17.160 --> 00:09:17.900
Uhm.

00:09:17.900 --> 00:09:23.900
I don't know if you can call this performing abroad, but this one time we were in the Canary Islands when I was around nine years old.

00:09:23.920 --> 00:09:24.680
With my family.

00:09:24.880 --> 00:09:25.760
That counts!

00:09:25.800 --> 00:09:26.640
Yes, that counts!

00:09:27.140 --> 00:09:30.920
And my mom was having a gig at this ...

00:09:31.120 --> 00:09:37.760
... Italian restaurant three nights in a row. And it was her together with this Elvis impersonator.

00:09:39.620 --> 00:09:40.840
And I ...

00:09:40.960 --> 00:09:43.440
... had just started my Elvis period.

00:09:43.440 --> 00:09:46.760
So I was walking around in Elvis clothes in the Canary Islands.

00:09:46.900 --> 00:09:54.400
And I asked: «Excuse me. Mom, do you think I can go up there and be Elvis with Elvis?»

00:09:54.660 --> 00:09:56.900
And she said that I should ask him.

00:09:57.620 --> 00:10:03.340
So I asked him before the show, being around eight years old, and he was like: «Yes, absolutely!»

00:10:03.340 --> 00:10:05.160
And he was like «Do you know how?», and I was like: «Yes, I can do this».

00:10:05.560 --> 00:10:16.940
So when I got up there, people started coming over from other restaurants, and in the end it was packed. And I did my Elvis thing.

00:10:17.060 --> 00:10:19.540
So the night after I got to do it again.

00:10:20.440 --> 00:10:22.780
And then I was one of the artists!

00:10:27.620 --> 00:10:29.740
That was my first ...

00:10:29.980 --> 00:10:31.980
... gig abroad, you could say!

00:10:31.980 --> 00:10:34.000
I've actually also performed in the Canary Islands!

00:10:34.180 --> 00:10:37.700
But I was the back side of a donkey. I was a horse's ass.

00:10:37.700 --> 00:10:39.720
In something called «Miniklubben».

00:10:39.720 --> 00:10:42.120
I wasn't asked back the night after.

00:10:42.560 --> 00:10:44.640
You didn't to a good enough job?

00:10:44.680 --> 00:10:46.580
I was inside the ass.

00:10:46.580 --> 00:10:51.260
There was one person in the front and one in the back. I was in the back, wagging the tail.

00:10:51.760 --> 00:10:54.840
You weren't good enough, since they didn't let you back?

00:10:54.840 --> 00:10:55.540
We only did it one night.

00:10:55.540 --> 00:10:56.220
It was one night only?

00:10:56.280 --> 00:10:57.560
Once upon a time ...

00:10:57.740 --> 00:10:59.820
Yeah, because that has to be ...

00:10:59.820 --> 00:11:03.140
... the biggest compliment you could get, is when you're ...

00:11:03.140 --> 00:11:04.540
... asked to do it again.

00:11:05.780 --> 00:11:08.820
We've got ...

00:11:09.200 --> 00:11:13.520
Before we continue the show, the two of you are gonna do a small ...

00:11:13.720 --> 00:11:16.400
A small medley, I think?

00:11:16.820 --> 00:11:20.580
I don't know more than that you've asked to get some ...

00:11:20.640 --> 00:11:22.000
We found out that ...

00:11:22.000 --> 00:11:23.700
Sorry, I just interrupted you ...

00:11:23.700 --> 00:11:24.760
But we found out that ...

00:11:25.160 --> 00:11:28.040
... our songs are in the same key.

00:11:28.160 --> 00:11:32.000
And they've almost got a similar vibe in the chords, so ...

00:11:32.000 --> 00:11:34.240
So we've found each other in the music!

00:11:34.240 --> 00:11:37.400
So Norway and Sweden are competing in Lisbon in the same key?

00:11:37.400 --> 00:11:38.420
Exactly!

00:11:38.580 --> 00:11:39.560
Is that a problem?

00:11:39.780 --> 00:11:42.220
No! It's 2018, baby!

00:11:42.440 --> 00:11:44.920
Let's get Benjamin's guitar in here!

00:11:44.980 --> 00:11:45.780
Okay, shit.

00:11:45.860 --> 00:11:49.060
So we ... Should we just ...

00:11:49.060 --> 00:11:52.460
It's fun that they're in the same key and that they're a little the same ...

00:11:52.600 --> 00:11:54.840
Let's see if they still are!

00:11:59.900 --> 00:12:02.940
I'll try to not sing falsetto this time, then.

00:12:48.080 --> 00:12:48.980
Fun!

00:12:49.500 --> 00:12:52.640
You'll meet again in Lisbon May 12th!

00:12:52.640 --> 00:12:55.200
Thanks so much for being here tonight!

